        <title type="html"><![CDATA[clarify visual authoring order vs mathematical application for transform property]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43496</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43496"/>
        <updated>2026-03-19T16:55:44.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120011256?u=9b1c1de5a62d4cc8a73582b6a58232dcfcca3188&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This PR clarifies the relationship between the written order of transform functions (left-to-right) and their mathematical application (right-to-left). It emphasizes that each function modifies the local coordinate system for subsequent functions, which is why the visual result follows the authoring order</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The current wording in the Values section ("effectively applied in order from right to left") creates a mental mismatch for developers. While mathematically true for point-mapping , it contradicts the visual intuition described in the Transform order section, where a rotation "tilts" the axes for a following translation. These changes bridge that gap by explaining that functions establish cumulative coordinate spaces.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">This clarification is based on the CSS Transforms Module Level 1 and 2 specifications:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-transforms-1/#transform-rendering:~:text=Multiply%20by%20each%20of%20the%20transform%20functions%20in%20transform%20property%20from%20left%20to%20right" rel="nofollow">Matrix Composition (L-to-R)</a>: The transformation matrix is computed by multiplying functions from left to right.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-transforms-1/#transform-rendering:~:text=Specifying%20a%20value%20other%20than%20none%20for%20the%20transform%20property%20establishes%20a%20new%20local%20coordinate%20system%20at%20the%20element%20that%20it%20is%20applied%20to.%20The%20mapping%20from%20where%20the%20element%20would%20have%20rendered%20into%20that%20local%20coordinate%20system%20is%20given%20by%20the%20element%E2%80%99s%20transformation%20matrix." rel="nofollow">Coordinate Systems</a>: Each function establishes a new local coordinate system for the element.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-transforms-1/#intro:~:text=Each%20%3Ctransform%2Dfunction%3E%20can%20get%20represented%20by%20a%20corresponding%204x4%20matrix.%20To%20map%20a%20point%20from%20the%20coordinate%20space%20of%20the%20div%20box%20to%20the%20coordinate%20space%20of%20the%20parent%20element%2C%20these%20transforms%20get%20multiplied%20in%20the%20reverse%20order%3A" rel="nofollow">Mathematical Application (R-to-L)</a>: Mapping a point from the element to the parent effectively happens in reverse order.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43180.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3970997824" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43180" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43180/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43180">#43180</a></p>


]]></content>
